\ Combinator-bounded call site in interpreter-free AOT mode. The metadata-
\ only image still carries the combinator slot table, so the combinator
\ satisfies-and-dispatch helper resolves the descriptor through the slot
\ table exactly as the runtime-image binary does -- with no interpreter
\ linked into the binary at all.
\
\ The intersection's addable element requires bump-it, so the combinator
\ provably guarantees the generic's method and the call site is bounded. No
\ bump-it method is registered for fixnum, so the check fails with a protocol
\ error and the binary exits with an error. The result is dropped rather than
\ printed: printing words still need interpreter fallback, which the locked
\ interpreter-free build rejects.

addable:   protocol{ bump-it: } ;
printable: protocol{ show-it: } ;
bump-it:   generic ( x: addable & printable -- n ) [ drop 0 ] ;

\ Combinator-bounded call site: compiled output emits the combinator
\ satisfies-and-dispatch helper.
bounded-caller: ( x: addable & printable -- n ) [ bump-it ] ;

1 bounded-caller drop
